# Build output. build.sh, build-deb.sh and build-rpm.sh all write here. Also
# ignore a bare `go build ./cmd/nbdash` run from the repo root, which drops a
# binary here named after the module rather than under dist/.
dist/
/nbdash

# ui/'s own build output. ui/vite.config.ts builds straight into
# internal/web/static/app/, which Go then embeds — see build.sh's comment on
# why that output is built fresh (by build.sh, or CI) rather than committed.
# Only the assets/ subdirectory is ignored, not index.html itself: a
# committed placeholder lives at internal/web/static/app/index.html so a
# plain `go build` still compiles even before anyone has run `npm run build`.
internal/web/static/app/assets/

# Local editor / agent configuration. The whole directory, not just the one
# file that used to be listed — a stray local settings file in a public repo
# leaks machine paths at best.
.claude/
.idea/
.vscode/

# Go
*.test
*.out
coverage.txt

# Environment files. deploy/nbdash.env.example is the tracked template; any
# real .env carries AUTH_CLIENT_SECRET and must never be committed.
*.env
!deploy/nbdash.env.example
